  "_commit": {
    "id": "1553c93227f2ef10e21277f4409e1e3097fc8efa",
    "author": "Patrick Aboyoun <aboyoun.patrick@gene.com>",
    "committer": "Patrick Aboyoun <aboyoun.patrick@gene.com>",
    "message": "Write an explicit null crs for an unknown CRS in writeGeoParquet()\n\nThe GeoParquet spec treats a missing \"crs\" key as OGC:CRS84 and spells\n\"unknown\" as an explicit \"crs\": null. writeGeoParquet() omitted the key\nwhen st_crs(x) was NA, so readers labeled coordinates with no CRS (e.g.\nspatial omics tissue coordinates) as WGS84 lon/lat, which then altered\naxes in plots and geometric operations.\n\nAn unknown CRS, or one PROJJSON cannot represent, is now written as\n\"crs\": null and reads back as NA. The append = TRUE CRS check likewise\ndistinguishes a missing key from an explicit null, so a known CRS can no\nlonger be appended to a file whose CRS is unknown. jsonlite needs\nnull = \"null\" to emit the null; its default writes [{}].\n\nAn existing test asserted that an unset CRS round-trips to the CRS84\ndefault rather than NA; it now expects NA. Files written by earlier\nversions have no \"crs\" key and still read as CRS84.\n",
    "time": 1794597475
  },
